Dear Bethany and Ruth,

Indeed the role of autocorrelations for the Method of Moments is unrelated to the multiplication factor which is used for maximum likelihood estimators (both ERGM and for the longitudinal SAOM) and currently not yet in RSiena. 

The proof of the pudding is in the convergence t-ratios produced in phase 3. If these are small enough, it does not matter if autocorrelations during phase 2 are high. 

Best wishes,

Tom

