Dear Maarten,

Sorry, this was my fault: if you have missing values, sum needs to be told
to exclude them, and I forgot to tell you this. After a while you see the
NA and react immediately: Oh dear, I forgot "na.rm=TRUE" e.g.

sum(use, na.rm=TRUE)

to select a range, use %in%:

use <- shy %in% 1:4

%in% is kind in that it does not insist you remove missing values. The
alternative

use <- shy > 0 & shy < 5

would need

use <- is.na(shy) & shy > 0 & shy < 5

Regards,

Ruth
